    "id": "ANAT-001-000001-I",
    "subject": "Anatomy",
    "text": "What are the site and the timing of the origin of the primordial germ cells?",
    "explanation": "Primordial germ cells originate in the epiblast, during the 2nd week of development. Primordial germ cells (PGCs) are also known as primitive sex cells. During the 2nd week of development, they originate in the epiblast at the caudal end of the primitive streak. They are the precursors of gametes in both genders. They pass through the primitive streak during gastrulation and reach the wall of the yolk sac. They migrate from the yolk sac in the 4th week and reach the developing gonads by the end of the 5th week.",
