    "id": "ANAT-001-000004-I",
    "subject": "Anatomy",
    "text": "During which phase of meiotic division are leptotene and zygotene stages seen?",
    "explanation": "Leptotene and zygotene are stages of prophase 1 of meiosis I. Meiosis is a special type of cell division that reduces the chromosome number by half. It creates 4 daughter cells, each with haploid chromosomes distinct from the parent cell. Meiosis consists of two successive divisions called the first and second meiotic divisions. The various stages of meiosis are as follows: \r\nFirst meiotic division (meiosis I) \r\n• Prophase 1 (Leptotene, Zygotene, Pachytene, Diplotene, Diakinesis) \r\n• Metaphase 1 \r\n• Anaphase 1 \r\n• Telophase 1 \r\n\r\nSecond meiotic division (meiosis II) \r\n• Prophase 2 \r\n• Metaphase 2 \r\n• Anaphase 2 \r\n• Telophase 2",
