    "id": "ANAT-002-000004-I",
    "subject": "Anatomy",
    "text": "During fertilization, all of the following barriers in the ovum are penetrated by the sperm except:",
    "explanation": "The sperm does not penetrate the nuclear membrane of the oocyte. The three barriers for sperm penetration in the ovum include: \r\n• Corona radiata \r\n• Zona pellucida \r\n• Oocyte cell membrane \r\nAfter the fusion of the sperm and oocyte cell membranes, the nucleus of the ovum is converted to the female pronucleus. The nucleus of the sperm becomes the male pronucleus.",
