    "text": "The bilaminar embryonic disc is made up of which of the following cells?",
    "explanation": "The bilaminar embryonic disc is made up of the epiblast layer (columnar cells) near the amniotic cavity and the hypoblast layer (cuboidal cells) near the blastocyst cavity. On the 8th day of development, the embryoblast differentiates into two layers, hypoblast and epiblast, to form the bilaminar disc. Around the same time, a small amniotic cavity appears within the epiblast. At this stage, the two layers of embryoblast are arranged as follows: • One layer of high columnar cells known as the epiblast layer, adjacent to the amniotic cavity • One layer of small cuboidal cells known as the hypoblast layer, adjacent to the blastocyst cavity The image given below shows the embryonic disc with the epiblast and hypoblast layers.",
